@q 21:20

**Dry ice** is solid CO_{2} at -78.5°C; it **sublimes** directly into gas and is used to keep things cold in transport and for stage fog. **Nitrogen** (78%) is the main component of air, and **hydrogen** is used to make vanaspati ghee.

@section 16.2 | Hydrogen and Water

@q 22:1-2

**Hydrogen** makes up about **three-quarters of the ordinary matter** of the universe by mass; **helium** comes second. Burned, it gives only water, so it is the **cleanest fuel** (India's **National Green Hydrogen Mission**, 2023).

@q 22:3-5

**Heavy water** (D_{2}O, deuterium oxide) has a molecular mass of about **20** (ordinary water 18). It is used as a **moderator and coolant** in nuclear reactors. **Reverse osmosis** turns salt water into drinking water.

@q 22:6

@src1 22:1

**Hydrogenation**: hydrogen gas is passed through vegetable oil at about 150-200°C with finely divided **nickel** as a catalyst, turning unsaturated liquid oils into **semi-solid vanaspati**. It creates **trans fats**, which raise heart-disease risk; FSSAI limits trans fat to **2%** of oils and fats.

@section 16.3 | Noble Gases and Nitrogen

@q 23:1

@pyq U.P. R.O./A.R.O. (Mains) 2016; U.P. P.C.S. (Mains) 2014; U.P. Lower Sub. (Pre) 2004
Which of the following pair of gases is used for the respiratory activities of divers?
(a) Oxygen and Nitrogen
(b) Oxygen and Helium
(c) Oxygen and Argon
(d) Oxygen and Neon
@ans (b)
@note The source prints the option labels out of order; the intended answer, as its explanation says, is **oxygen and helium**.
@end
@src 23:2

Deep-sea divers breathe **heliox** (helium + oxygen) because helium, unlike nitrogen, dissolves little in blood under pressure, which avoids **nitrogen narcosis** and the **bends** (decompression sickness).

@q 23:3-7

@table
Gas | Use / fact
**Helium** | Balloons and airships (light and **non-flammable**), diving gas, cooling MRI magnets (liquid helium)
**Neon** | Red-orange advertising signs
**Argon** | Filling electric bulbs and tube lights; welding shield
Krypton, xenon | Special lamps, camera flashes
**Radon** | Radioactive; cancer therapy; seeps from soil
**Nitrous oxide** (N_{2}O) | **Laughing gas**, anaesthetic; also a greenhouse gas
Nitric oxide (NO) | Pollutant; a signalling molecule in the body
**Nitrogen** | **Aircraft tyres** (dry, inert, steady pressure), packaging chips, preserving food; liquid N_{2} (-196°C) for freezing
**Ammonia** | Extremely **soluble in water**; fertilisers, refrigeration
@end

**Actinium** is a radioactive metal (an actinide), not a noble gas. **Bordeaux mixture** (copper sulphate + lime) is a fungicide, and **boric acid** is an antiseptic. Nitrogen fixation and denitrification balance each other in the **nitrogen cycle**, so total nitrogen in air and land stays about the same.

