A gas is lighter than air if its molar mass is **below about 29**: hydrogen (2), **helium (4)**, methane (16), ammonia (17) and neon (20) are lighter; HCl (36.5), SO_{2} (64), CO_{2} (44) and chlorine (71) are heavier.

@q 23:10

**Bromine** is the only **non-metal liquid** at room temperature; **mercury** is the only liquid metal.

