@table
pH | Substance
0-1 | Battery acid, HCl in the **stomach (about 1.5-2)**
2-3 | Lemon juice, vinegar
4.5-5.5 | **Acid rain** (below 5.6), black coffee
About 6.5 | Milk, saliva (6.5-7.5)
**7** | **Pure water** (neutral, at 25°C)
**7.35-7.45** | **Human blood** (slightly basic)
About 8 | Sea water, baking soda solution
10-11 | Milk of magnesia, soap
12-14 | Lime water, **caustic soda**
@end

pH below 7 is **acidic** and above 7 is **basic**; both statements in the 2025 question are reversed.

@q 24:2-3

**Aqua regia** ("royal water") is **3 parts concentrated HCl + 1 part concentrated HNO_{3}**; it dissolves **gold and platinum**, which no single acid can.

