@src 24:9

@q 24:10-13

Black-and-white film carries **silver bromide**; light reduces it, and **hypo** (sodium thiosulphate) dissolves the unexposed salt to "fix" the image. **Lithium** salts (the question's "lithium bicarbonate") are used for **bipolar disorder**, and older texts mention them for rheumatism.

@trap
**Graphite**, not diamond, is the most stable form of carbon. **Graphene = single carbon layer.** **Fullerene has no fluorine.** **Anthracite** has the most carbon; **pig iron** has the most carbon among irons. Heavy water's molecular mass is **20**. **Vanaspati = hydrogenation** with a nickel catalyst. **Laughing gas = nitrous oxide (N_{2}O)**, not nitric oxide. **Divers: helium + oxygen.** Acids have pH **below** 7. **Aqua regia = HCl + HNO_{3} (3 : 1).** **Baking soda = NaHCO_{3}**, washing soda = Na_{2}CO_{3}. **Bleaching powder = calcium oxychloride.** **Hypo = sodium thiosulphate.**
@end

@heatmap

@pattern
The **2023-2025** papers asked several basic chemistry questions each year in statement form (pH, baking soda, gases lighter than air, noble gases). Common names and uses of salts are the most repeated sub-topic across all years, followed by allotropes of carbon.
@end

